--- THG2-06: a whole thing interpolates into a format string ---
a cairn called i1.
Set i1's 'the chain length' to -0027.
Print i1.
Print "the north offset reading: {i1}".

--- the same leaf, nested ---
  a cairn called i2,
  Set i2's 'the chain length' to -0027,
  Print i2,
  Print "the north offset reading: {i2}".

--- THG2-08, THG2-09: is / is not between two things ---
a cairn called i3.
a cairn called i4.
If i3 is not i4 then, Print "ASSERT THG2-08: expected i3 to equal i4", Exit 95. Print i3.
Set i4's 'the chain length' to -00027.
If i3 is i4 then, Print "ASSERT THG2-09: expected i3 to differ from i4", Exit 95. Print i3.

--- THG2-10: the comparison recurses into a nested field ---
a waypoint called i5.
a waypoint called i6.
Set i5's height's 'the chain length' to -00027.
If i5 is i6 then, Print "ASSERT THG2-10: expected i5 to differ from i6", Exit 95. Print i5.
Set i6's height's 'the chain length' to -00027.
If i5 is not i6 then, Print "ASSERT THG2-10: expected i5 to equal i6", Exit 95. Print i5.

--- THG2-21: an ordinary global function taking a thing, both call forms ---
a cairn called i7.
Set i7's 'the chain length' to -000027.
a number called c1 is 'the balance so far' of i7.
If c1 is not 729 then, Print "ASSERT THG2-21: expected 729 got {c1}", Exit 95. Print c1.
a number called c2 is i7's 'the balance so far'.
If c2 is not 729 then, Print "ASSERT THG2-21: expected 729 got {c2}", Exit 95. Print c2.

--- THG2-27: of / to / with / on all introduce arguments ---
a cairn called i8.
Set i8's 'the chain length' to -000027.
a number called c3 is 'chalk the score' on i8 and 378.
If c3 is not -10206 then, Print "ASSERT THG2-27: expected -10206 got {c3}", Exit 95. Print c3.
a number called c4 is 'chalk the score' of i8 and 378.
If c4 is not -10206 then, Print "ASSERT THG2-27: expected -10206 got {c4}", Exit 95. Print c4.
a number called c5 is 'chalk the score' to i8 and 378.
If c5 is not -10206 then, Print "ASSERT THG2-27: expected -10206 got {c5}", Exit 95. Print c5.
a number called c6 is 'chalk the score' with i8 and 378.
If c6 is not -10206 then, Print "ASSERT THG2-27: expected -10206 got {c6}", Exit 95. Print c6.

--- THG2-30: the receiver fills the first parameter, the rest follow the preposition ---
a cairn called i9.
Set i9's 'the chain length' to -000027.
a number called c7 is i9's 'chalk the score' on 378.
If c7 is not -10206 then, Print "ASSERT THG2-30: expected -10206 got {c7}", Exit 95. Print c7.

--- THG2-32: a receiver reached through a field reads the same way ---
a waypoint called i10.
Set i10's height's 'the chain length' to -000027.
a number called c8 is i10's height's 'the balance so far'.
If c8 is not 729 then, Print "ASSERT THG2-32: expected 729 got {c8}", Exit 95. Print c8.

--- THG2-70: is a <type> recognises the six builtins ---
a text called c9 is 'roll it along' of 9223372036854775807.
If c9 is not "number" then, Print "ASSERT THG2-70: expected number got {c9}", Exit 95. Print c9.

--- the same leaf, nested ---
  a text called c10 is 'roll it along' of 9223372036854775807,
  If c10 is not "number" then, Print "ASSERT THG2-70: expected number got {c10}", Exit 95. Print c10.

--- a program with no things at all: every gen_thing_fn_*-dependent leaf stands aside ---
Print 0 minus 0.

--- the reset fix: seed 1 (has things) run immediately before seed 4 (has none) in one process ---
thing fn ready after a things-free program: 0
nested-receiver ready after a things-free program: 0
Print 0 minus 0.

--- THG2-70's predicate function stays available even with zero things ---
predicate ready with no things: 1
a text called c11 is 'gather up' of true.
If c11 is not "boolean" then, Print "ASSERT THG2-70: expected boolean got {c11}", Exit 95. Print c11.

